{
  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that for PCA RNA, multiprofile with avgpool is much stronger than singleprofile and also stronger than transformer aggregation, with both accuracy and F1 supporting this. The major remaining uncertainty is whether the image modality provides useful signal at all, and whether the same profile/aggregation setting transfers to image features. config_011 tests an image-only ResNet-50 baseline under the currently promising multiprofile/avgpool setting, changing mainly the modality relative to config_002. This gives a necessary unimodal image baseline before testing fusion, helping isolate whether image features are informative rather than confounding image usefulness with fusion strategy or RNA encoder choice."
}

